From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?=
 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 07:20:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand the visible product and device names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium -> colorburst, and the device is a "computer" rather than a
Chromebook or a "Chrome device". Both flow through placeholders that every
screen already substitutes, so one edit per name covers OOBE, the login
screen and Settings in all 248 locales without touching a translation:

  IDS_PRODUCT_NAME / IDS_SHORT_PRODUCT_NAME              -> colorburst
  IDS_{,SHORT_,INSTALLED_}PRODUCT_OS_NAME                -> colorburst
  IDS_*_DEVICE_NAME{,_IN_PLURAL}                         -> computer(s)
  IDS_ASH_MESSAGE_CENTER_SYSTEM_APP_NAME                 -> colorburst

The product names were translated as themselves, so dropping their old
translation ids is right: a brand should not be localised. The device names
were not, so ui_chromeos_strings_vi.xtb gains the two entries that keep the
Vietnamese UI Vietnamese ("máy tính"), keyed by the grit fingerprint of the
new English source.

The Google "G" that headed 28 OOBE screens is replaced by a colorburst mark
-- the reference bars a colour television locks its phase to. One icon
definition, and the screens pick it up by name.

Our own local-account strings no longer mention Google at all: the card reads
"Create a local account / An account that stays on this computer. No internet
connection needed."

Verified on a booted image: welcome, install-or-try and account screens all
read colorburst / máy tính, with the bars in place of the G.

